# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# music-miles — "Tracks" — onboarded 2026-10-17 at James's music-miles#1
#
#   "Can you onboard these projects onto kit even if you don't start working
#   on them yet" … "I am kind of thinking just call it "Tracks" with a tag line
#   of track your tracks tracks"
#
# The repo is empty, so there is no code to infer from. Everything here comes
# from what he has written on music-miles#1: a running app that puts the music
# you listened to onto the route you ran. The corpus keeps the repo's name
# until the repo is renamed (renaming it is his call); the product name is in
# BEH-BRAND-1.
#
#   DEFINED   — his words on music-miles#1. Cites the issue.
#   INFERRED  — my reading of the idea, or a detail it needs that he hasn't
#               stated. Each is `review unreviewed`: it shows in Proposed, and
#               he can deny it. Some lean on the Gemini reply he pasted there,
#               which he has not endorsed line by line.
#
# Nothing is built. `kit check music-miles` names every behaviour as missing.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

feature FEAT-BRAND "Name and voice"
feature FEAT-CONNECT "Connecting Strava and Spotify"
feature FEAT-MAP "The music map of a workout"
feature FEAT-SHARE "Sharing a workout"


# ═══ DEFINED — music-miles#1 ═══

behaviour BEH-BRAND-1 "The app is called Tracks, and its tagline is: Track your tracks' tracks"
  in FEAT-BRAND
  layer ux
  source defined music-miles#1
  review unreviewed
  priority 1
  actor runner
  when opens page:Home
  then sees region:Hero
  contract "just call it "Tracks" with a tag line of track your tracks tracks": a running track, a GPS track and a music track
  contract unreviewed because he wrote "kind of thinking"; the name and the repo rename stay his


# ═══ INFERRED — what the idea needs ═══

behaviour BEH-CONNECT-1 "A runner connects their Strava account so Tracks can read their workouts"
  in FEAT-CONNECT
  layer ux
  source inferred music-miles#1
  review unreviewed
  priority 1
  actor runner
  when opens page:Connect
  when activates button:ConnectStrava
  then sees region:Workouts
  contract read-only: Tracks never writes to Strava unless BEH-SHARE-2 is approved

behaviour BEH-CONNECT-2 "A runner connects their Spotify account so Tracks can read what they listened to"
  in FEAT-CONNECT
  layer ux
  source inferred music-miles#1
  review unreviewed
  priority 1
  actor runner
  when opens page:Connect
  when activates button:ConnectSpotify
  then sees region:Workouts
  contract read-only: Tracks reads listening history and never controls playback

behaviour BEH-MAP-1 "Each workout shows the songs played during it, pinned along its route"
  in FEAT-MAP
  layer ux
  source inferred music-miles#1
  review unreviewed
  priority 1
  actor runner
  given workout:WithSongs
  when opens page:Workout
  then sees region:RouteMap
  then sees region:SongList
  contract each song sits on the map at the point where it started, shown by its cover art
  contract the list below the map shows the same songs in order, with the distance each one covered

behaviour BEH-MAP-2 "A song is placed on the route by matching when it played to where the runner was"
  in FEAT-MAP
  layer technical
  source inferred music-miles#1
  review unreviewed
  priority 1
  actor runner
  contract a song belongs to a workout when it started between the workout's start and end
  contract its pin is the route point whose timestamp is nearest the song's start
  contract a workout with no songs in its window still shows its route, with no pins

behaviour BEH-MAP-3 "A workout recorded without GPS lists its songs but draws no map"
  in FEAT-MAP
  layer ux
  source inferred music-miles#1
  review unreviewed
  priority 2
  actor runner
  given workout:Indoor
  when opens page:Workout
  then sees region:SongList
  contract treadmill and indoor workouts have time but no route, so songs are listed by elapsed time

behaviour BEH-SHARE-1 "A workout can be saved as a share card: the route with the song covers on it"
  in FEAT-SHARE
  layer ux
  source inferred music-miles#1
  review unreviewed
  priority 2
  actor runner
  given workout:WithSongs
  when opens page:Workout
  when activates button:Share
  then sees region:ShareCard
  contract sized for an Instagram or Strava story, from the Gemini reply he pasted
  contract minimal and high-contrast: the word TRACKS, the route line, the covers

behaviour BEH-SHARE-2 "The songs can be written into the Strava activity's description"
  in FEAT-SHARE
  layer technical
  source inferred music-miles#1
  review unreviewed
  priority 3
  actor runner
  contract only when the runner turns it on: it is the one write Tracks would make to Strava
